# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Biome's formatter is configured `lineEnding: "lf"` and treats a CRLF file as unformatted, so with
# `core.autocrlf=true` — the Windows default — a fresh clone fails `pnpm lint` before a single edit.
# Measured: a CRLF `package.json` is reported by `biome check` as needing every line rewritten.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated by packages/tokens and compared byte for byte against a fresh run. A line-ending rewrite
# would break that comparison.
apps/web/src/styles/theme.css text eol=lf

# Binary: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.gif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.ico binary

# Collapsed by default in review, still expandable. Not `-diff`: a lockfile diff is how an unexpected
# transitive dependency gets caught, and CONTRIBUTING.md requires a justification for every new one.
pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated
